    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math lessons by adapting to individual learning paces, providing instant feedback on problems, and generating relatable examples. For instance, they could explain complex topics like calculus using analogies from everyday life or literature. This makes abstract concepts more accessible and engaging for diverse learners."
